From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:28:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: synchronize bandwidth in AP/STA support

When an AP follows a co-located station (repeater), the channel of
the station alone is not enough: the AP must also adopt its
bandwidth. wpa_supplicant reports the control frequency, channel width
and 320 MHz block of the driver chandef on channel switch events and
in the status. An MLO association has no interface chandef, so the
status reports each link from its own chandef in the interface query.
That query leaves the link state of the driver alone, so a later link
addition still finds the new link. A link without a chandef reports
its BSS frequency and HT secondary channel offset, and the AP keeps
its configured width. The per-link reporting follows
mtk-openwrt-feeds 7a38cb57511c ("[openwrt-25][MAC80211][WiFi7][Prepare
for Filogic 880/850 MP4.3 release]").

hostapd uses the reported width instead of its configured widths only
when present, because ucode evaluates null >= 0 as true. hostapd
computes segment 0 and the center frequency for every width,
including 20/40 MHz and the second 320 MHz block. A running AP
applies a change of only the segment center or the width, for example
between the two 320 MHz blocks. Without a width, the channel
computation fails instead of using 20 MHz. A missing or invalid
320 MHz block falls back to the first one.

Based-on-work-by: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
